<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33308" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαία</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάα,</span>
		ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>olive-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i>, esp. in <i><span class="en">Od., 11.590</span></i>,
			al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱερὴ ἐ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				13.372
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				3.13
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.55
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				701
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρη ἐλαίη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.82
				</span></i>
			 (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγρία ἐ</span>. or <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κότινος</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> φέρεσθαι
				ἐκτὸς τῶν ἐλαῶν</span> to run beyond <i>the
			olives</i>, which stood at the end of the Athenian racecourse, i.e.
			to go too far, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				995
			</span></i>, ubi v. Sch.; of the Indian <i>Olea
			cuspidata</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.4.11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> variety of 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάφνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					111
				</span></i>
			, ib.<i><span class="en">
				4.7.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				16.3.6
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>olive</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				550
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				372c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.262
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.119
			</span></i>, etc.—Acc. to Gramm. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάα</span> was the proper form in this sense, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλαία</span> in the first; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάα</span> is simply the 
				Att.
			 form, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.94.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.476.21
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1055.36
			</span></i> (also <i><span class="en">
				<u>PHal.</u>
				1.98
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>naevus on the skin</i>, Melamp.<i><span class="en">
				p.508F.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίφρου Κυρηναϊκοῦ
				μέρος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> [In <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάα</span>, the penult. is
			long, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				360.46
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				550
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				578
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Av.</u>
				617
			</span></i>, etc.; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλᾰῶν</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				261.3
			</span></i> (where perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλῶν—ἐλᾶς</span> is acknowledged by <i><span class="en">
				Ael.Dion.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				162
			</span></i>, and found in <i><span class="en">
				<u>PRyl.</u>
				97.7
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλᾶν</span> in
				<i><span class="en">
				130.11
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>—should be restored), and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span> in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλάη</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				4.2.12
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Phil.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				6.102
			</span></i> (Id.).]</div>
